{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לאחרונה יסעו", :translit "le'acharonah yisa'u", :gloss "at the rear they shall travel"} {:he "יהיה להם זכרון", :translit "yihyeh lahem zikharon", :gloss "there shall be for them a remembrance"} {:he "המן", :translit "haman", :gloss "Haman"} {:he "פסל מיכה", :translit "pesel mikha", :gloss "idol of Micah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לאחרונה"]} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "יהיה להם זכרון", :spells "המן"}], :frame {:text "When Israel journeyed, the tribe of Dan traveled last, at the rear — 'מאסף לכל המחנות' (Numbers 2:31). Because the tribe of Dan hosted Micah's idol (Judges 18), Amalek, who attacks the stragglers 'זנב כל העדה הלכים אחריכם' (Deuteronomy 25:18), mutilated them. Haman, descended from Amalek, sought 'להשמיד להרוג ולאבד את כל היהודים' (Esther 3:13).", :sources ["Numbers 2:31" "Judges 18" "Deuteronomy 25:18" "Esther 3:13"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לא התפקדו בתוך בני ישראל", :translit "lo hitpakdu betokh benei yisra'el", :gloss "they were not counted among the children of Israel"} {:he "תגין", :translit "tagin", :gloss "crowns"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Tagin on the letter heh signal a masoretic note about five censuses from which this group was excluded"}], :frame nil}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לאחרונה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "לאחרונה", :refs ["Numbers 2:31" "Ecclesiastes 1:11"], :n 2, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :sofei-tevot, :phrase "יהיה להם זכרון", :spells "המן", :letters ["ה" "ם" "ן"], :by :selah, :order :in-order} {:kind :other, :note "Tagin on the letter heh signal a masoretic note about five censuses from which this group was excluded", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:26:51.478046631Z", :model "glm-5.2"}